summary:
Wall Street ended higher on Tuesday as easing concerns over oil supply helped support market sentiment, while strong import demand pointed to resilient economic activity and kept inflation and Fed policy expectations in focus. The Nasdaq Composite, the Dow and the S&P 500 ended in positive territory.

How Did the Benchmarks Perform?

The Dow Jones Industrial Average (DJI) rose 0.5%, or 253.14 points, to close at 51,521.04. Twenty-one components of the 30-stock index ended in positive territory;
